# The memory card prompts with no card at all (drive.py's default
# --no-card), from the memory card scene: "There is no Memory Card in Slot
# A." with its key, queued behind the startup's ready line; A asks
# "Continue without saving or loading Game Data?" with OK hovered and the
# keys, the run's first prompt with a choice; Right says "Try Again", and A
# on it says the missing card again. A and OK then go on to the opening
# movie.
#   python tools/a11y/drive.py tools/a11y/memcard_no_card.drive --scene ""

wait 'speak queue \(off\): "There is no Memory Card in Slot A\. A to continue\."$'
press A
wait 'speak interrupt \(off\): "Continue without saving or loading Game Data\? OK\. Left and Right choose, A confirms\."$'
press Right
wait 'speak interrupt \(off\): "Try Again"$'
press A
wait 'speak interrupt \(off\): "There is no Memory Card in Slot A\. A to continue\."$'
press A
wait 'speak interrupt \(off\): "Continue without saving or loading Game Data\? OK\."$'
press A
wait '"Opening movie\. Press Start to skip\."$'
